**Why do some people still feel like outsiders even after living abroad for 10 years?**

Having worked in New Zealand, Australia, China, Japan, the US, and the UK, I've noticed an interesting phenomenon: some people speak excellent English but struggle to truly integrate, while others, whose English isn't perfect, quickly build relationships. Why? This is a question I've been pondering lately.
